---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import SignalGrid from '../ui/SignalGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s43-observability"
  chapter="Observability"
  title="Signals — WHAT, WHY, WHEN, WHERE"
  notes="Kubernetes tells you WHAT happened; other signals tell you WHY, WHEN, WHERE, and HOW MUCH. Walk SignalGrid: events are free and fast, logs are narrative, metrics are trends, traces are paths. Profiling: which code path under load. Don't reach for traces when events already explain the scheduling failure. Next slide: stack mapping (Prom/Grafana/Loki/Tempo/OTel)."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-8">
    <SignalGrid
      items={[
        { label: 'Events — WHAT', value: 'What changed? Who acted? (scheduler, kubelet, probe)' },
        { label: 'Logs — WHY', value: 'Why did it fail? Stack traces, config, app narrative' },
        { label: 'Metrics — WHEN', value: 'When did it start? How bad? Rate, saturation, SLO burn' },
        { label: 'Traces — WHERE', value: 'Where is latency? Which hop dropped the request?' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-deck-border bg-deck-panel/60 p-6">
      <div class="mb-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-amber">
        Profiling — HOW MUCH in code
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg text-deck-text/90">
        CPU / heap flame graphs — <span class="text-deck-muted">Which code path consumes resources under load?</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <Callout type="rule">
      Events explain Kubernetes actions; logs explain application failures. Metrics confirm timing. Traces locate the hop.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
